# What is deliberately NOT in this repo.
#
# `_dev/` used to be ignored wholesale. That single line is why the build
# tooling was never tracked and had to be force-added in August 2026. Ignore
# only the scratch inside it, never the directory.

# Watcher runtime state. publish.sh writes these while it runs and relies on
# them being ignored -- .watch-heartbeat is touched every 5 seconds, so if it
# were tracked the watcher would commit and push in a loop forever.
_dev/.watch-heartbeat
_dev/.publish-error
_dev/*.log

# The DCA licensee cache. `_dev/dca_licensees.py` downloads California's
# monthly file of every BBS licensee here - 35MB, 165,000 records, and it
# carries ADDRESSES. For a solo practitioner the address of record is usually
# their home. This repository publishes to GitHub Pages, so a tracked copy is a
# public copy within two minutes.
#
# The pass checks this line exists and refuses to download without it. Do not
# remove it. Only the derived counts in _dev/dca_stats.py are ever committed.
_dev/_cache/

# Local-only scratch
_dev/local.html
_to_delete/
_publish/

# Machine noise
.DS_Store
*.fuse_hidden*
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Abandoned mockups and build output that duplicates the live site.
# Regenerate with mock/mftguide/build_schools.py if ever needed.
mock/landing/
mock/mftguide/schools/

# Deploy tarballs. The cloud session ships a build as a tar.gz into _dev/,
# extracts it, and moves it to _to_delete/. On 17 Aug 2026 the watcher
# committed one before the extract finished, putting a 7MB binary blob into
# history for nothing. The window is real - the watcher polls on its own
# clock - so the file must never be committable in the first place.
_dev/*.tar.gz
